e":230,"path":231,"stem":232},"Player Tracker Rework","\u002Fdesign\u002Fplayer-tracker-rework","9.design\u002Fplayer-tracker-rework",{"title":234,"path":235,"stem":236},"Qualifications","\u002Fdesign\u002Fqualifications","9.design\u002Fqualifications",{"id":238,"title":221,"body":239,"description":8,"extension":312,"links":313,"meta":314,"navigation":315,"path":222,"redirect":313,"seo":316,"stem":223,"__hash__":317},"content_en\u002F9.design\u002Fdb-sync.md",{"type":240,"value":241,"toc":305},"minimark",[242,250,255,262,266,296,300],[243,244,245,249],"p",{},[246,247,248],"strong",{},"Status",": Implemented",[251,252,254],"h2",{"id":253},"goal","Goal",[256,257,258],"ul",{},[259,260,261],"li",{},"Multi-Framework compatibility - \"Abstracting\" the framework's tables away via a separate sync process with handles\u002Fmerges the data as needed into FiveNet compatible table structure.",[251,263,265],{"id":264},"idea","Idea",[267,268,269,277,280,283],"ol",{},[259,270,271,272],{},"Sync process that takes care of reading and transforming the data.\n",[267,273,274],{},[259,275,276],{},"Cleanup of deleted, e.g., users, vehicles, etc., should be handled as well.",[259,278,279],{},"Config presets for common frameworks (e.g., ESX, QB)",[259,281,282],{},"For communicating changes from FiveNet to the gameserver, the NATS websocket system or a custom websocket system could be used (messages would be encoded via Protobuf JSON).",[259,284,285,286,290,291],{},"A \"state\" file (like log collectors use to store the \"last line\") to store the last \"ID\" (in case of tables without an ID field, it would use, e.g., the ",[287,288,289],"code",{},"owner"," field).\n",[267,292,293],{},[259,294,295],{},"In case of multiple queries, the state is stored per query index number in the config file.",[251,297,299],{"id":298},"limitations","Limitations",[256,301,302],{},[259,303,304],{},"Only one (main) phone number per char\u002Fuser.",{"title":306,"searchDepth":307,"depth":307,"links":308},"",2,